Z||000006||The Fieromaster||07-11-2001||11:56 PM||||There are allotta hop ups for the gun.. best is a remote tank adapter.. to put the tank on your belt rather than on the gun - lighter smaller gun!  Also you can get a better feeding hopper... one with a motorized piece inside to stop blockages!  Also lighter double finger triggers rule!  Coolest hop up is a electronic grip that you can set firing rates on.. auto or semi auto, burst, and pasword protected saftey!!  Bad A$$ toys!!<P>I had a pro light too... i like my Piranha better though its more acurate and lighter, but id dunno if my Piranha is as good as the Tipmans in the long run.  Tipman is a GOOD reliable company!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||10
Z||000007||Pontiaddict||07-12-2001||01:06 AM||||I knew about the tank adapter and the motorized hopper. That electronic grip sounds cool, but this gun needs the basics upgraded before that. It's basically a step up from one of the base model guns.||||reg||1
Z||000008||The Fieromaster||07-12-2001||01:12 AM||||Well i believe you already have the basic stuff from the factory.. that would be a venturi bolt (for better flow).. the only other upgrade you dont have is a turbo valve!  The are better flowing firing valves!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That, Wrecked Better"<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">      <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||07-12-2001||04:59 AM||||Nope, no venruri bolt, no ram air chamber not turbo valve, no expansion chamber, Basically the only option on the gun was the bottom line adapter.<BR>I think I'll get the expansion chamber, then the bolt, then the valve. (eventually) I don't need to dump too much money into this gun when all I'm going up against are Spyders.||||reg||1
